            [ 'Who gets the $250 Trump account deposit?', 'According to Invest America, 25 million children born from January 1, 2016 through December 31, 2024 who live in ZIP codes with a median family income of $117,300 or less, plus eligible children on military bases. The cutoff is based on the ZIP code’s Census data, not your own income. All deposits were made as of October 9, 2026.' ],
            [ 'Why did the Dell income threshold change from $150,000?', 'The December 2025 announcement used ZIP codes with median incomes below $150,000. After Treasury auto-enrolled every eligible child, many more children qualified, so the same $6.25 billion was allocated from the lowest-income ZIP codes upward until 25 million children were reached. The final cutoff was a median family income of $117,300 or less.' ],
            [ 'What is the Trump account 530A employer match?', 'Section 530A defines Trump accounts, and section 128 lets employers contribute through a separate written plan. Up to $2,500 a year per employee is excluded from the employee’s income, counted across all of the employee’s children. Employer money counts toward the $5,000 yearly limit. Ask HR whether your employer offers a program.' ],
